# Tips of the day on the simple dashboard (docs/profile.md, docs/i18n-design.md): short,
# practical and judgment-free. Revision: AI draft, not yet reviewed by a native speaker. Who each
# tip is for (level, goal and income type in the profile) stays in the code, in content/tips.ts.

dicas-anotar-logo = Writing down an expense right after you make it helps you not forget. It's like taking a photo of the receipt.
dicas-reserva-com-pouco = Start your emergency fund small: 50 a month already makes a difference. What matters is the habit.
dicas-guarde-primeiro = Save first, spend later: as soon as money comes in, set aside the part for your emergency fund.
dicas-gastos-pequenos = Small expenses that repeat (coffee, delivery, apps) add up to a lot by the end of the month. It's worth checking how much it was.
dicas-juros-mais-altos = If you have more than one debt, pay off the one with the highest interest first (like a credit card balance) and keep paying the minimum on the others.
dicas-renda-variavel = If your income changes from month to month, plan the month around the lowest amount that usually comes in. Anything extra goes to your emergency fund.
dicas-beneficios = Benefits that arrive on the same day every month help you plan: note the day and set aside the fixed bills first.
dicas-assinaturas = Check your subscriptions once a month: it's common to pay for something you no longer use.
dicas-meta = For a goal (a trip, a renovation), divide the amount by the months until the date: it's easier to know how much to save each month.
dicas-comparar-mes = Compare this month with the previous one: the category that grew the most is usually the best place to save.
